Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.20,0:00:03.07,Caption,,0,0,0,,Energy gets wasted for a boring reason:
Dialogue: 0,0:00:03.21,0:00:06.90,Caption,,0,0,0,,nobody trusts the forecast enough to act on it.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.20,0:00:08.87,Caption,,0,0,0,,In September 2026, I built Agentic Arbiter.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.01,0:00:11.40,Caption,,0,0,0,,It covers 238 real data-centre campuses across 36 US states.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.70,0:00:13.57,Caption,,0,0,0,,Data centres run chillers even when
Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.71,0:00:15.90,Caption,,0,0,0,,the air outside is already cold enough.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.00,0:00:21.20,Caption,,0,0,0,,It works hour by hour, deciding when it's safe to shut the chillers off.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.50,0:00:23.43,Caption,,0,0,0,,It made no unsafe calls.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.57,0:00:25.50,Caption,,0,0,0,,The old controller made one.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.80,0:00:29.50,Caption,,0,0,0,,Over five real years, that's about four hundred extra hours a year.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:29.80,0:00:30.88,Caption,,0,0,0,,And it grades itself.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:31.02,0:00:34.78,Caption,,0,0,0,,Here it's missing its target, because the data was patchy during the hackathon window.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.92,0:00:36.00,Caption,,0,0,0,,It says so itself.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:36.30,0:00:39.67,Caption,,0,0,0,,Second of 842 teams, out of nearly four thousand people,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:39.81,0:00:41.84,Caption,,0,0,0,,at FortyGuard's hackathon, sponsored by NVIDIA.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.98,0:00:44.00,Caption,,0,0,0,,The UN-backed Cool Coalition featured it.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:44.30,0:00:48.00,Caption,,0,0,0,,Next I want it running live on real sites, not just measured on them.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:48.30,0:00:49.45,Caption,,0,0,0,,Then I looked at home.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:49.59,0:00:52.59,Caption,,0,0,0,,Pakistan has solar on millions of roofs, but the grid can't see it.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.73,0:00:55.50,Caption,,0,0,0,,Go over two hundred units a month, and every unit gets re-priced.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.80,0:00:57.04,Caption,,0,0,0,,I asked twenty-one families.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:57.18,0:01:01.50,Caption,,0,0,0,,Seven of the ten with solar have changed habits or are getting a battery.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:01.80,0:01:03.86,Caption,,0,0,0,,So I'm building a Solar Home Agent.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:04.00,0:01:08.70,Caption,,0,0,0,,It helps most in a solar home with no battery that can't sell its spare power.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:09.00,0:01:14.70,Caption,,0,0,0,,It reads tomorrow's weather, picks when to run the motor and the iron, and remembers how wrong it's been.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:15.00,0:01:19.59,Caption,,0,0,0,,Moving a few jobs into the sunny hours keeps this home under the limit.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:19.73,0:01:21.70,Caption,,0,0,0,,About five thousand rupees this month.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:22.00,0:01:23.67,Caption,,0,0,0,,Nearly nineteen thousand over the next six.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:23.81,0:01:26.20,Caption,,0,0,0,,It's a simulation, on one real month of Islamabad weather.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:26.50,0:01:30.01,Caption,,0,0,0,,Thirteen said they'd only trust an app that explains itself.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:30.15,0:01:31.20,Caption,,0,0,0,,So mine does.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:31.50,0:01:34.21,Caption,,0,0,0,,When it isn't sure, it says no,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:34.35,0:01:35.90,Caption,,0,0,0,,and tells you why.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:36.20,0:01:38.90,Caption,,0,0,0,,It keeps score against what the sun actually did.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:39.20,0:01:41.97,Caption,,0,0,0,,But look what it can't fix: it still wastes most of its midday sun,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:42.11,0:01:42.90,Caption,,0,0,0,,and buys after dark.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:43.20,0:01:45.40,Caption,,0,0,0,,Storage closes that.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:45.70,0:01:49.10,Caption,,0,0,0,,Next: five to ten homes in Islamabad, over WhatsApp.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:49.24,0:01:53.40,Caption,,0,0,0,,Then add them into one neighbourhood forecast, with our distribution company.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:53.70,0:01:55.86,Caption,,0,0,0,,The solar is already on Pakistan's roofs.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:56.00,0:01:59.40,Caption,,0,0,0,,I want to help the grid see it, and trust it.
